notes: The owner explicitly requested V031 while V030 had not been separately accepted, so V030 is the previous candidate and V024 / 0_2_4 remains the owner-confirmed passed baseline. V031 preserves all seven V030 network comparison modes and their protected timing behavior while adding schema-versioned persistent normalized decision evidence. Scenario, cooperation, pedestrian-awareness, vehicle-class, emergency-priority and emergency-lifecycle histories are projected into one compact ledger with deterministic evidence IDs, action/decision/reason, timing before/after, relevant context, provenance, concise explanations and source references. New JSON/CSV evidence endpoints can also project the schema on demand for older stored network runs without rewriting them. Same-candidate repair: pedestrian max-wait starvation prevention now suppresses ordinary cooperation/class extensions until pedestrian service begins, while emergency priority remains separately bounded; cooperation/pedestrian/class/emergency detailed events also retain previous/effective timing so normalized evidence can reconstruct timing changes. Second same-candidate conflict repair: the network benchmark now uses an explicit one-owner-per-intersection policy arbiter (incident hold > active pedestrian crossing > simulated emergency priority > pedestrian max-wait > configured class priority > cooperation), post-advisory signal reads use non-reapplying snapshots so ranked scenarios are evaluated once per tick, and protected-service requests carry source/priority/lifecycle metadata and clear when service begins. The seven comparison modes remain ablation modes; V031 does not claim that class-aware and emergency-priority overlays run together in one integrated mode. Physical/public-road traffic control remains disabled.
